nodecode-levea-video is a rewrite of brajendrak00068's brajendrak00068/agentic-ai-video-production:

  https://github.com/brajendrak00068/agentic-ai-video-production
  commit 0f11f14511c8b9a030689d1541c28752c1d60a59
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 brajendrak00068 (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the five tools and their whole call path -- levea_video_edit
(POST /execute), levea_queue_edit (POST /queue-edit), levea_job_status
(GET /jobs/{id}, with its wait loop up to ten minutes), levea_task_status
(GET /task-status/{id}) and levea_active_task (GET
/projects/{id}/active-task, whose answer signals a running edit with a
typed `active` flag instead of a success flag); the request fields the
plugin read out of its edit_contract.json, declared here as two boundary
contracts (the full edit, and the queued one that requires a project), so
the schema the model reads and the body the backend receives come off one
declaration; the params / projectId / top-level placement of those
fields; the read of the outcome from the backend's own `success`,
`partial`, `verificationPassed` and status rather than from HTTP 200; the
which-states-are-pending and which-are-terminal tables; the per-profile
settings for the key (an inline secret or the environment variable it
names), the API host with its path normalisation, the default project and
the timeouts; and the skill's edit -> poll -> follow-up guidance, kept as
the :levea manual topic and the tool descriptions.

Left out: the bundled SKILL.md file as a separate registered skill, because
a cell's prose guidance is its manual topic and its tool descriptions (the
words survive, the file loader does not); and the plugin's Hermes-only
registration surface -- the toolset, emoji and secret-scope plumbing --
which is the cell declaration's own job here. The Hermes per-profile
plugin-data directory and plugin.yaml settings became the cell's
levea-video config section, and the tools answer text led by the state and
the ids instead of the bare JSON object the plugin returned, because a
model reads the state first.
